### Chapter 4: Functional Requirements
4.1 Introduction

This chapter specifies the functional requirements of the Distributed Web-Based Chat Application. Functional requirements describe the services, operations, and behaviors that the system shall provide to its users. Each requirement is uniquely identified to facilitate traceability during system design, implementation, testing, and maintenance. The system follows a modular architecture in which authentication, messaging, user management, media handling, notifications, and distributed communication operate as independent yet interconnected services. Every function described in this section is essential to ensuring that the application provides a secure, scalable, and reliable real-time messaging experience.

The application shall allow multiple users to communicate simultaneously through a distributed infrastructure while maintaining message consistency, minimizing latency, and ensuring secure access to system resources. Functional requirements are categorized into logical modules to simplify implementation and future expansion.

4.2 User Registration Module

The user registration module enables new users to create an account within the application. Registration serves as the initial step before users can access messaging features. During registration, users shall provide their full name, username, email address, and password. The system shall validate all input fields before creating the account.

The application shall verify that the supplied email address is unique within the database. Duplicate registrations using an existing email address shall not be permitted. Passwords shall never be stored in plain text. Before storage, passwords shall be encrypted using the bcrypt hashing algorithm with an appropriate salt factor.

Following successful registration, the system shall generate a verification token and send an email verification request to the user's registered email address. Until verification is completed, restricted access policies may be applied according to system configuration.

Upon successful registration, a user profile shall be created automatically with default settings including profile image, online status, privacy preferences, notification settings, and account metadata.

The registration service shall record the account creation timestamp, IP address (optional), and device information for auditing purposes.

