4.3 User Authentication Module

Authentication ensures that only authorized users gain access to protected resources. The application shall implement secure login using email and password authentication combined with JSON Web Tokens (JWT).

During login, the system shall retrieve the user's encrypted password from MongoDB and compare it against the submitted password using bcrypt. If authentication succeeds, a short-lived access token and a long-lived refresh token shall be generated.

Access tokens shall authorize API requests while refresh tokens enable seamless session renewal without requiring repeated login. Expired access tokens shall not permit access to protected endpoints.

The authentication service shall also support secure logout functionality by invalidating refresh tokens and terminating active sessions.

Multiple devices shall be supported, allowing users to remain logged in across desktop and mobile browsers independently.

The system shall detect invalid login attempts and temporarily restrict repeated authentication failures to prevent brute-force attacks.

