# 12.8 Group Management APIs

Group APIs enable collaborative communication involving multiple participants. Authenticated users create new groups, modify group information, invite participants, remove members, assign administrative roles, and retrieve group details.

Administrative privileges determine which operations individual users may perform. Group owners possess complete administrative authority, while moderators receive limited management capabilities according to assigned permissions.

Invitation endpoints generate notifications informing selected participants about pending invitations. Membership changes immediately trigger Redis synchronization events ensuring distributed consistency.

Future application versions may extend these APIs to support community management, announcement channels, event scheduling, and collaborative workspaces.

