# 12.9 File Management APIs

File management endpoints support uploading, downloading, previewing, and deleting multimedia content shared throughout conversations.

Uploaded files undergo validation according to permitted formats, maximum file sizes, MIME types, and security policies before transfer to cloud object storage. MongoDB stores descriptive metadata rather than binary file contents.

Successful uploads return publicly accessible storage references together with associated metadata including filenames, upload timestamps, file sizes, and preview information where applicable.

Download operations verify user authorization before granting access to stored resources, ensuring that only conversation participants retrieve protected content.

