Administrative endpoints remain accessible exclusively to authorized system administrators. These interfaces provide infrastructure monitoring, user management, audit log retrieval, application configuration, moderation activities, and system diagnostics.

Administrative APIs expose operational metrics describing backend health, database performance, Redis utilization, WebSocket activity, authentication statistics, and infrastructure availability.

Security-sensitive operations including account suspension, configuration modification, and infrastructure maintenance require elevated authorization verification before execution.

Comprehensive audit logging records every administrative activity for accountability and security analysis.

