# 15.5 Limitations of the Current System

Although the proposed application satisfies project objectives, several practical limitations remain.

The current implementation focuses primarily on real-time messaging rather than integrated voice or video communication. Multimedia collaboration therefore remains limited compared with comprehensive enterprise communication platforms.

End-to-end encryption has not been implemented within the initial version. Although communication occurs securely through HTTPS and authentication mechanisms remain protected, server-side message storage remains necessary for synchronization and persistence.

Horizontal scalability currently depends upon Redis Pub/Sub synchronization. Extremely large deployments involving millions of concurrent users may eventually require more sophisticated distributed messaging technologies such as Apache Kafka or partitioned event streaming architectures.

Offline message synchronization remains limited because the application currently assumes continuous Internet connectivity during active communication.

Native desktop and mobile applications are outside the scope of the present implementation. Users access the system primarily through modern web browsers.

Despite these limitations, the architecture intentionally accommodates future expansion without requiring significant redesign.

